{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1440943-on-the-subject-of-a-mage-the-ascension-jrpg","id":1440943,"title":"On the subject of a Mage the Ascension JRPG","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-03-22T07:31:31-07:00","id":1440943,"title":"On the subject of a Mage the Ascension JRPG","content":"Recenlty I've been listening to Kikuo, his music and the cover art of his albums gives me a lot of Mage vibes as well as specifically Marauder vibes, his music is like the OST to a Marauder JRPG, which has inspired me to write up this page and ask: What would a Mage: the Ascension JRPG look like? Ponder this after you've read my notes on this subject<br /> <br /> 1st: in mage games there are 3-5 players. This hypothetical game should reflect this by having 4-5 party members. JRPGs like Delta Rune, Undertale, Parisite Eve, OMORI (I think), Lisa the joyfull, Hylics, Suits (I think), and other show you don't need an ensemble cast whose party members you have to switch out to make a JRPG.<br /> <br /> 2nd: Mages are glass cannons. all it takes is 1 well placed bullet or a few bullets in general to kill a mage. Party members should consist of the few mages who can take as much as they dish out such as Akashics, Hermetics/Etherites who can built Armor, R<span style=\"font-size:13px\">evenant Mages, Cyborg mages, Matrix mages who are modelled after NEO from the Matrix</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">3rd: This game should have an OV ala the persona games.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">4th: This game should have an optional secret boss who is the hardest boss in the game. I nominate Vormas - harvester of souls<br /> <br /> 5th: The OST should be done by either Kikuo, Toby Fox, Shoji Meguro, Perdro Silva, or come combination of all these artist. I'm open to other suggestions<br /> <br /> 6th: the story should focus on a newly awakened mage and whoever they manage to recruit into their party. I envision orphans but I'm open to other suggestions. all that's neccesary for the story is for it to start off upbeat and for the story to slowly and by degrees get darker and for the stakes to get higher.</span><br /> <br /> 7th: as for an engine: I'd like the engine used in the persona games to make it feel like a JRPG, Failing that, I like the Unreal engine, alternativly, there a lot of good RPG maker games so having the RPG maker engine is not out of the question. I hear bad things about Unity so that engine should be avoided in my oppinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26433-ascentionthemage","name":"AscentionTheMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26433_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-22T07:43:42-07:00","id":1440945,"title":"","content":"For some reason I want this song to be the music for the OV: <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/track/7pKd9l7ef8BoII1NQREB6G?si=FXOAs7WUQl-Fs9MT_g9OLg\" target=\"_blank\">https://open.spotify.com/track/7pKd9...Ql-Fs9MT_g9OLg</a><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">Also it would be ideal if a Mage artist did the character portraits. I personally love John Van Fleets work, although I'm not sure if he can do bright upbeat art. Shigenori Soejima is probably too busy with Persona 6 or another persona spin off so let's not bother him.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26433-ascentionthemage","user":"AscentionTheMage","date":". 03-22-2021, 12:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"